WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:11.966
Lumiose City! We're back again!

2
00:00:12.033 --> 00:00:14.500
- Pika!
- We get to see Clemont, too!

3
00:00:14.566 --> 00:00:16.800
Denne-denne-ne!

4
00:00:16.866 --> 00:00:19.500
- So Ash. Ready to go?
- You bet!

5
00:00:19.566 --> 00:00:22.366
- Ready to battle.
- Pika. Pikachu.

6
00:00:22.433 --> 00:00:24.233
Clemont?

7
00:00:25.433 --> 00:00:29.166
- Pika!
- Ches! Chespin! Pin!

8
00:00:29.233 --> 00:00:31.600
- Hey, Clemont!
- I'm back! Yay!

9
00:00:31.666 --> 00:00:35.266
- I'm so glad that you're back!
- It's a pleasure to see everyone again.

10
00:00:35.333 --> 00:00:37.433
Thanks! It sure has been a while.

11
00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:39.700
So, Bonnie, how's everything been going?

12
00:00:39.766 --> 00:00:42.466
Awesome! Looks like everything's going good for you too.

13
00:00:42.533 --> 00:00:44.233
Denne-ne-ne-ne-ne!

14
00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:46.600
You're not gonna believe all the nice girls

15
00:00:46.666 --> 00:00:49.133
I've been asking to take care of you.

16
00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:51.233
- Uh!
- So many keepers!

17
00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:53.233
So much has happened since you left!

18
00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:55.000
Now, just calm down.

19
00:00:55.066 --> 00:00:56.866
You can tell me about it later. Deal?

20
00:00:56.933 --> 00:01:00.933
You don't have to tuck me in any more when I go to sleep.

21
00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:03.966
- Serena does it now. Right?
- Right.

22
00:01:04.033 --> 00:01:07.333
So what do you say? Ready for me to challenge the Lumiose Gym?

23
00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:11.700
- Yeah! Totally ready!
- Huh. Oh, yeah.

24
00:01:11.766 --> 00:01:13.733
Look! Braixen, come on out!

25
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:19.366
Wow, Fennekin evolved into Braixen!

26
00:01:19.433 --> 00:01:20.600
Braixen!

27
00:01:20.666 --> 00:01:25.366
Fennekin was exceptionally cute, of course, but Braixen is beautiful!

28
00:01:25.433 --> 00:01:26.966
What do you think, Chespin?

29
00:01:27.033 --> 00:01:28.533
Chespin! Che!

30
00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:30.833
We've been practising our new performance routine.

31
00:01:30.900 --> 00:01:34.466
Now that you have Braixen, you'll come up with all sorts of new things.

32
00:01:34.533 --> 00:01:38.133
- Right!
- Oh, yeah. Check this out! Unh.

33
00:01:39.666 --> 00:01:41.233
Goodra. Goodra!

34
00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:44.966
- Your Sliggoo evolved into Goodra?
- Uh-huh.

35
00:01:45.033 --> 00:01:49.400
It's a lot stronger. I'm all set for our battle!

36
00:01:49.466 --> 00:01:50.933
Pikachu.

37
00:01:51.066 --> 00:01:52.866
♪ You're just a kid on a quest ♪

38
00:01:52.933 --> 00:01:54.633
♪ To be the best of the best ♪

39
00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:58.066
♪ Someday you're destined for power and glory ♪

40
00:01:58.133 --> 00:01:59.533
♪ You know you're up to the test ♪

41
00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:03.433
♪ There's only one way to tell this story ♪

42
00:02:03.500 --> 00:02:06.700
♪ Be a hero! Be a hero! ♪

43
00:02:06.766 --> 00:02:10.133
♪ All the power is at your command ♪

44
00:02:10.199 --> 00:02:14.100
♪ Face your fears and show you're a hero ♪

45
00:02:14.166 --> 00:02:18.800
♪ The future of the world is in your hand! ♪

46
00:02:18.866 --> 00:02:21.066
♪ Pokémon! ♪

47
00:02:23.766 --> 00:02:26.033
Confronting the Darkness!

48
00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:34.400
Our heroes have finally arrived in Lumiose City,

49
00:02:34.466 --> 00:02:37.566
where Ash hopes to win his fifth Kalos Gym Badge.

50
00:02:37.633 --> 00:02:41.466
And his opponent will be his friend Clemont, the Lumiose Gym Leader!

51
00:02:41.533 --> 00:02:46.166
I hope you're ready for this, cos I know I'm gonna win my fifth Gym Badge!

52
00:02:46.233 --> 00:02:48.500
Well, I'm not gonna make it easy for you!

53
00:02:48.566 --> 00:02:51.833
I'm so excited to finally watch Ash and Clemont's Gym Battle!

54
00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:53.266
- Hmm.
- Rex.

55
00:02:53.333 --> 00:02:54.800
Cham!

56
00:02:54.866 --> 00:02:56.766
And Clemont came back home early.

57
00:02:56.833 --> 00:02:58.666
Just to make sure he was all set.

58
00:02:58.733 --> 00:03:01.500
- Isn't that right, Dedenne?
- Denne, denne.

59
00:03:01.566 --> 00:03:06.233
It's time to begin this Lumiose City Gym Battle challenge!

60
00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:08.566
What do you say we get things going?

61
00:03:08.633 --> 00:03:11.900
You betcha!

62
00:03:13.733 --> 00:03:14.833
Officer Jenny?

63
00:03:15.766 --> 00:03:17.033
Pika. Um... Hi there.

64
00:03:17.100 --> 00:03:20.166
You must be Clemont, the Lumiose City Gym Leader.

65
00:03:20.233 --> 00:03:22.133
- Is that right?
- Right.

66
00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:24.666
Then that must be Clembot?

67
00:03:24.733 --> 00:03:28.500
Uh, yes... Is there a problem, officer?

68
00:03:28.566 --> 00:03:31.400
We were just getting an important battle started.

69
00:03:31.466 --> 00:03:35.300
Clembot, look at this. You're under arrest!

70
00:03:35.366 --> 00:03:37.800
Clembot's under arrest?

71
00:03:37.866 --> 00:03:39.833
-Pika.

72
00:03:42.066 --> 00:03:47.600
What did I do wrong? I assure you I am completely innocent, sir!

73
00:03:47.666 --> 00:03:50.633
I know, Clembot. It must be some kind of mistake.

74
00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:51.933
Don't worry.

75
00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:54.833
I promise I'll prove your innocence, no matter what it takes!

76
00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:57.866
Please try to relax while we sort this whole thing out.

77
00:03:57.933 --> 00:04:00.733
- Denne.
- All right. I'll try.

78
00:04:02.033 --> 00:04:05.766
Strange things have been happening in Lumiose City lately.

79
00:04:05.833 --> 00:04:08.566
First, there's the sign on our three-star hotel.

80
00:04:08.633 --> 00:04:11.133
Somebody stole one of its stars!

81
00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:14.233
Next, there is the incident where all the mannequins on display

82
00:04:14.300 --> 00:04:17.733
at a high-end boutique were found hanging upside down

83
00:04:17.800 --> 00:04:20.200
and wearing bathing suits.

84
00:04:20.266 --> 00:04:22.800
No doubt there's been some weird stuff going on,

85
00:04:22.866 --> 00:04:25.266
but what does Clembot have to do with this?

86
00:04:25.333 --> 00:04:28.233
- Pikachu.
- Look at these.

87
00:04:28.300 --> 00:04:31.000
They're surveillance videos.

88
00:04:31.066 --> 00:04:33.466
- Oh, no.
- It's proof positive.

89
00:04:33.533 --> 00:04:37.533
Would you mind zooming in a little bit closer?

90
00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:41.166
See that? I know Clembot has a dent on the top of its head.

91
00:04:41.233 --> 00:04:43.333
But this robot doesn't have one!

92
00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:45.866
I'm afraid this video doesn't prove that.

93
00:04:45.933 --> 00:04:48.600
So you're saying that it's definitely Clembot?

94
00:04:48.666 --> 00:04:50.100
Officer Jenny. Wait.

95
00:04:50.166 --> 00:04:54.833
I can vouch for Clembot's innocence because I've been with Clembot constantly!

96
00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:57.400
Alibis provided by friends aren't reliable.

97
00:04:57.466 --> 00:05:01.733
And with all the evidence I have, I'll have to make an arrest.

98
00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:03.300
- Uh...
- So all we have to do

99
00:05:03.366 --> 00:05:06.666
- is prove that Clembot's innocent, right?
- Right.

100
00:05:08.566 --> 00:05:11.733
I tell you, I am an innocent robot. Innocent!

101
00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:16.733
Son!

102
00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:19.066
- Dad!
- Daddy!

103
00:05:19.133 --> 00:05:22.866
It’s my sweet Bonnie! Welcome home! It’s good to see all of you.

104
00:05:22.933 --> 00:05:24.466
It's nice to see you.

105
00:05:24.533 --> 00:05:26.466
So they’ve arrested Clembot?

106
00:05:26.533 --> 00:05:30.033
- Clembot did nothing wrong!
- Right. I know that!

107
00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:31.700
Guys!

108
00:05:33.533 --> 00:05:35.266
Alexa!

109
00:05:36.233 --> 00:05:38.066
- Videos?
- Yes.

110
00:05:38.133 --> 00:05:41.266
They're of the three-star hotel and high-end boutique incidents.

111
00:05:41.333 --> 00:05:43.433
They were caught by security cameras.

112
00:05:43.500 --> 00:05:47.033
And both videos show a robot who looks just like Clembot.

113
00:05:47.100 --> 00:05:50.333
- But it's not Clembot!
- Of course. I know that.

114
00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:53.466
So I've been looking into those incidents on my own.

115
00:05:53.533 --> 00:05:58.633
During my research, I discovered the man in the Blaziken mask is involved.

116
00:05:58.700 --> 00:06:00.400
Blaziken Mask? No way.

117
00:06:00.466 --> 00:06:04.566
It seems he's trying to get to the bottom of this as well.

118
00:06:04.633 --> 00:06:09.433
Uh... Heh. You're not serious, are you? You're saying Blaziken Mask is real?

119
00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:12.733
Yeah. And he's always with his Mega Blaziken.

120
00:06:12.800 --> 00:06:17.100
Uh, Mega Blaziken? Well, that's a new one on me.

121
00:06:17.166 --> 00:06:20.100
It's true! Blaziken Mask had helped us before!

122
00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:28.800
That Blaziken Mask just might have some kind of lead.

123
00:06:28.866 --> 00:06:32.133
-Those videos are all we have.

124
00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:33.300
At least for now.

125
00:06:33.366 --> 00:06:36.866
All I can think of is it was made to look just like Clembot.

126
00:06:36.933 --> 00:06:39.233
But they'd need blueprints.

127
00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:42.300
They wouldn't be able to make Clembot without them, right?

128
00:06:42.366 --> 00:06:44.900
- Right.
- So tell me, where are the blueprints?

129
00:06:44.966 --> 00:06:47.400
I filed them up in Prism Tower.

130
00:06:47.466 --> 00:06:49.100
They're saved on the computer there.

131
00:06:49.166 --> 00:06:53.000
Then I suggest you go there now and see if you can find any leads.

132
00:06:53.066 --> 00:06:56.033
- Right!
- Meanwhile, I'll see what I can find out.

133
00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:58.100
That would be great.

134
00:06:58.166 --> 00:07:00.900
We're gonna prove Clembot had nothing to do with this!

135
00:07:00.966 --> 00:07:02.966
- For sure!
- All right!

136
00:07:03.033 --> 00:07:04.833
- Denne, denne!
- Pika, pika!

137
00:07:08.366 --> 00:07:09.966
- What's up?

138
00:07:10.033 --> 00:07:13.233
I've uncovered concrete evidence that this computer's been hacked.

139
00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:15.000
So, what about the blueprints?

140
00:07:18.133 --> 00:07:21.300
It appears somebody located and copied all of them!

141
00:07:21.366 --> 00:07:24.100
Then that means Alexa was right all along.

142
00:07:24.166 --> 00:07:26.466
- Now hold on just one sec.
- Huh?

143
00:07:26.533 --> 00:07:30.566
If I can trace the computer that hacked into this one in the first place...

144
00:07:30.633 --> 00:07:32.266
You can do that?

145
00:07:35.400 --> 00:07:39.700
Apparently this shows the hackers were working from Lumiose University

146
00:07:39.766 --> 00:07:42.900
on the robotics department's server.

147
00:07:44.366 --> 00:07:49.533
Ah-ha! Clembot's blueprints! This proves they stole them from there!

148
00:07:49.600 --> 00:07:53.033
They even stole Clembot's operating system!

149
00:07:53.100 --> 00:07:56.500
Ah! That's it! The robot in the videos!

150
00:07:56.566 --> 00:07:58.933
It looks exactly like Clembot!

151
00:07:59.000 --> 00:08:03.433
- Like Clembot's got an evil twin.
- And that means that Clembot's bad.

152
00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:08.266
It says electronics storage.

153
00:08:08.333 --> 00:08:11.300
Look at that! It's the Lumiose Museum!

154
00:08:11.366 --> 00:08:15.800
- Lumiose Museum?
- Maybe they're gonna hit it next.

155
00:08:15.866 --> 00:08:18.033
That's a distinct possibility.

156
00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:20.800
Let's make a copy and give it to Officer Jenny!

157
00:08:22.833 --> 00:08:25.833
-Huh.

158
00:08:26.466 --> 00:08:30.833
It says "Belmondo". Is that a name?

159
00:08:38.900 --> 00:08:43.433
All right then, Dark Clembot. Let's do this with more of a kick today.

160
00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:46.200
Understood, master.

161
00:08:50.733 --> 00:08:52.700
Now, Magneton, use Discharge!

162
00:08:52.766 --> 00:08:55.633
Magneton!

163
00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:02.166
All right. Here we go.

164
00:09:06.300 --> 00:09:09.200
All the latest electronics are stored here!

165
00:09:09.266 --> 00:09:11.766
Perfect for raising some Team Rocket cash.

166
00:09:11.833 --> 00:09:13.800
But there's something we hadn't bargained for.

167
00:09:15.266 --> 00:09:18.900
A Pokémon-controlling robot. Bonus time!

168
00:09:18.966 --> 00:09:20.800
Tailor-made for Team Rocket.

169
00:09:20.866 --> 00:09:24.133
Well, then. Let's grab it and go!

170
00:09:24.200 --> 00:09:26.066
Righty-ho!

171
00:09:26.133 --> 00:09:28.266
Who's that Pokémon?

172
00:09:33.133 --> 00:09:35.600
It's Magneton!

173
00:09:35.666 --> 00:09:37.800
Magneton!

174
00:09:41.966 --> 00:09:45.233
It looks exactly like Clembot.

175
00:09:45.300 --> 00:09:47.666
We gave the surveillance footage a closer look.

176
00:09:47.733 --> 00:09:49.500
There was no dent on its head.

177
00:09:49.566 --> 00:09:51.900
Because it isn't Clembot. I tried to tell you!

178
00:09:51.966 --> 00:09:56.500
You see? That robot is the one who did all that horrible stuff!

179
00:09:56.566 --> 00:09:59.166
That possibility can't be ruled out.

180
00:09:59.233 --> 00:10:03.133
So tell me, Clemont, where did you get ahold of this data?

181
00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:05.900
I discovered someone hacked into the Prism Tower computer

182
00:10:05.966 --> 00:10:07.933
and stole Clembot's blueprints.

183
00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:10.233
I kept tracing it further and further back

184
00:10:10.300 --> 00:10:14.133
- until I found the keyword "Belmondo."
- Doctor Belmondo?

185
00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:16.733
- Is that name familiar?
- Of course.

186
00:10:17.933 --> 00:10:19.733
He's a robotics researcher.

187
00:10:19.800 --> 00:10:23.266
And he stole blueprints from the Prism Tower computer?

188
00:10:23.333 --> 00:10:25.366
- I'll investigate.
- One more thing.

189
00:10:25.433 --> 00:10:26.833
- Huh?
- Please have a look at this.

190
00:10:26.900 --> 00:10:30.333
These are the floor plans for an electronics warehouse.

191
00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:33.266
Oh, no! Another incident just occurred there!

192
00:10:33.333 --> 00:10:35.033
-What happened?

193
00:10:37.133 --> 00:10:40.866
- Oh, no.
- Those electronics were burnt to a crisp.

194
00:10:40.933 --> 00:10:45.066
- That's awful.
- And this situation is only getting worse.

195
00:10:45.133 --> 00:10:48.600
Uh! That's right! He had Lumiose Museum files, too!

196
00:10:48.666 --> 00:10:50.333
The Lumiose Museum?

197
00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:52.033
If they're going to strike again,

198
00:10:52.100 --> 00:10:54.900
it's possible that they'll target the museum next.

199
00:10:54.966 --> 00:10:57.833
Right. So that proves Clembot's innocent.

200
00:10:57.900 --> 00:11:01.133
- Please release Clembot.
- Hm.

201
00:11:01.200 --> 00:11:04.933
Officer, please! The only one who can stop Fake Clembot is Clembot,

202
00:11:05.000 --> 00:11:07.433
- and you know it!
- All right. I will.

203
00:11:07.500 --> 00:11:08.633
-Pika!

204
00:11:11.200 --> 00:11:14.900
- Sorry for the trouble I caused.
- OK. You're free to go.

205
00:11:14.966 --> 00:11:16.700
I'm so happy!

206
00:11:16.766 --> 00:11:18.833
Clembot, please.

207
00:11:18.900 --> 00:11:21.766
- We need your help right away!
- Sir.

208
00:11:21.833 --> 00:11:24.200
The real criminal needs to be caught, now!

209
00:11:24.266 --> 00:11:26.200
I'm happy to help!

210
00:11:26.266 --> 00:11:28.900
All right! It's all for one!

211
00:11:34.300 --> 00:11:37.033
I've already notified the museum officials.

212
00:11:37.100 --> 00:11:41.133
The most important thing to remember is you must stay hidden and quiet.

213
00:11:41.200 --> 00:11:43.600
We'll strike once they're caught in the act!

214
00:11:43.666 --> 00:11:46.466
- Let me know if anything comes up.
- We will!

215
00:11:53.700 --> 00:11:55.833
- Huh?
- Pika?

216
00:11:55.900 --> 00:11:58.300
-Pi.

217
00:11:58.366 --> 00:12:01.533
Oh! Look! Up there!

218
00:12:08.666 --> 00:12:11.000
All right. Time to work, Dark Clembot.

219
00:12:11.066 --> 00:12:13.100
Understood.

220
00:12:21.700 --> 00:12:25.466
- So you're Belmondo!
- Huh? Who are you?

221
00:12:25.533 --> 00:12:29.233
This monster was trying to sneak inside the Lumiose Museum!

222
00:12:29.300 --> 00:12:33.233
Just what are you planning to do with that fake Clembot?

223
00:12:33.300 --> 00:12:37.100
To frame your robot as a common criminal. Simple as that.

224
00:12:38.333 --> 00:12:41.600
- I'll go and get Officer Jenny right now.
- OK.

225
00:12:42.600 --> 00:12:47.533
Mark my words. I make the very best robots the world has ever seen.

226
00:12:47.600 --> 00:12:51.133
From the moment I saw your Clembot, I knew it wasn't complete.

227
00:12:51.200 --> 00:12:53.800
And that's when I realised what needed to be done.

228
00:12:53.866 --> 00:12:57.733
So I did it. My Dark Clembot is robot perfection!

229
00:12:57.800 --> 00:13:01.366
The greatest robot that has ever been created!

230
00:13:01.433 --> 00:13:03.200
You couldn't be more wrong.

231
00:13:03.266 --> 00:13:05.966
My Clembot is a masterpiece of robotic design!

232
00:13:07.333 --> 00:13:08.333
Think what you want,

233
00:13:08.400 --> 00:13:10.400
but there's no doubt you've ruined my ambition

234
00:13:10.466 --> 00:13:14.066
to frame your robot and have Dark Clembot be the hero

235
00:13:14.133 --> 00:13:16.466
who catches him and saves the day!

236
00:13:16.533 --> 00:13:20.233
So now we must battle to find out which robot is best.

237
00:13:20.300 --> 00:13:23.366
Let's see which robot is truly the greatest!

238
00:13:23.433 --> 00:13:25.866
You used the magnificent power of science

239
00:13:25.933 --> 00:13:28.033
to fulfil your own selfish ambitions.

240
00:13:28.100 --> 00:13:29.600
I'll take you on!

241
00:13:29.666 --> 00:13:31.400
Look what we have here.

242
00:13:31.466 --> 00:13:34.333
- A Pokémon battle.
- Magneton, go!

243
00:13:36.166 --> 00:13:37.200
Magneton.

244
00:13:37.266 --> 00:13:40.366
All right, then. Clembot, I'm counting on you!

245
00:13:40.433 --> 00:13:44.200
Understood, sir! Heliolisk, come out!

246
00:13:46.166 --> 00:13:47.300
Lisk!

247
00:13:50.866 --> 00:13:52.666
Thunder Shock, let's go!

248
00:13:52.733 --> 00:13:53.966
Magneton!

249
00:13:54.033 --> 00:13:57.466
- Heliolisk, dodge!
- Use Electro Ball!

250
00:13:57.533 --> 00:13:58.833
Magneton!

251
00:13:58.900 --> 00:14:01.566
Now use Dragon Tail for your counter-attack!

252
00:14:01.633 --> 00:14:05.300
Heliolisk!

253
00:14:05.366 --> 00:14:08.266
- Magneton, Tackle!
- Magneton!

254
00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:10.566
- Ton!
- Heliolisk!

255
00:14:10.633 --> 00:14:12.466
-Pika!

256
00:14:13.100 --> 00:14:15.666
- Lisk, helio!
- Heliolisk!

257
00:14:15.733 --> 00:14:19.000
Huh? Huh?

258
00:14:19.066 --> 00:14:20.866
He... heli...

259
00:14:20.933 --> 00:14:24.633
Doctor Belmondo and Dark Clembot! You two are coming with me.

260
00:14:24.700 --> 00:14:27.633
I have a few questions.

261
00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:30.233
Do it, Magneton!

262
00:14:30.300 --> 00:14:32.733
- Use Flash Cannon!
- Magneton!

263
00:14:32.800 --> 00:14:35.333
Dodge and use Parabolic Charge!

264
00:14:37.000 --> 00:14:38.000
Heli!

265
00:14:38.066 --> 00:14:40.100
Use Tackle, Magneton!

266
00:14:40.166 --> 00:14:42.933
- Magneton!
- Helio...

267
00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:48.233
- Heliolisk, no!
- Heli!

268
00:14:48.300 --> 00:14:51.233
You're slow, Magneton! Pick up the pace!

269
00:14:51.300 --> 00:14:54.333
- All right. This battle is over!
- Over?

270
00:14:54.400 --> 00:14:55.866
You've already lost.

271
00:14:55.933 --> 00:14:59.800
Your robot couldn't care less about the condition of your Pokémon one bit!

272
00:14:59.866 --> 00:15:01.866
All it cares about is winning!

273
00:15:01.933 --> 00:15:05.900
My Clembot always battles alongside my Pokémon!

274
00:15:08.366 --> 00:15:12.366
Oh, what a fool! The only thing that matters in battle is getting the win.

275
00:15:12.433 --> 00:15:14.466
That's how I programmed Dark Clembot.

276
00:15:14.533 --> 00:15:17.433
And that's what makes him the most powerful robot of all!

277
00:15:17.500 --> 00:15:19.066
Wrong, Belmondo!

278
00:15:19.133 --> 00:15:23.366
The robot who is best at Pokémon battling cares about Pokémon above all else!

279
00:15:23.433 --> 00:15:26.900
And that definition describes my Clembot to a tee!

280
00:15:26.966 --> 00:15:30.033
He's right! You lost, Belmondo!

281
00:15:30.100 --> 00:15:32.900
- Just give it up already!
- Pika, pika!

282
00:15:32.966 --> 00:15:34.933
Huh?

283
00:15:37.033 --> 00:15:39.233
Hey Clembot, what's wrong with you?

284
00:15:39.300 --> 00:15:41.900
Aaah! Aaah! Aaah!

285
00:15:43.533 --> 00:15:46.433
- Ah. What's with Clembot?
- Pika.

286
00:15:48.433 --> 00:15:50.833
What's with Clembot is what's with us!

287
00:15:50.900 --> 00:15:53.533
We've got a big magnet and that's a plus!

288
00:15:53.600 --> 00:15:55.866
To protect the world from devastation!

289
00:15:55.933 --> 00:15:58.700
To unite all people within our nation!

290
00:15:58.766 --> 00:16:01.733
To denounce the evils of no attraction!

291
00:16:01.800 --> 00:16:05.000
To extend our reach with magnetic action!

292
00:16:05.066 --> 00:16:07.000
- Jessie!
- And James.

293
00:16:07.066 --> 00:16:10.700
Team Rocket blasts off at the speed of light!

294
00:16:10.766 --> 00:16:13.566
Surrender now or prepare for an isotropic fight!

295
00:16:13.633 --> 00:16:15.433
Meowth, that's right!

296
00:16:17.166 --> 00:16:18.900
Team Rocket? Again?

297
00:16:20.600 --> 00:16:23.766
We attract technically advanced robots and repel twerps!

298
00:16:23.833 --> 00:16:27.333
At Team Rocket, naturally naughty behaviour is a way of life.

299
00:16:27.400 --> 00:16:30.900
And with this magnet, we can grab both of those metal heads at once!

300
00:16:30.966 --> 00:16:32.766
- What?
- Grrrr!

301
00:16:40.466 --> 00:16:43.300
- It's Blaziken Mask!
- And Mega Blaziken!

302
00:16:43.366 --> 00:16:46.466
- Ash!
- Alexa!

303
00:16:46.533 --> 00:16:48.566
- It's Blaziken Mask! See?
- Yeah.

304
00:16:48.633 --> 00:16:51.566
I won't let you cause any trouble for this city!

305
00:16:51.633 --> 00:16:53.300
Blaziken! Blaz!

306
00:16:54.366 --> 00:16:58.600
- Use Flare Blitz!
- Blaziken!

307
00:17:00.766 --> 00:17:03.300
- Use Blaze Kick! Now!
- Blaz!

308
00:17:06.700 --> 00:17:07.566
We're blasting...

309
00:17:07.633 --> 00:17:09.300
- Off...
- Again!

310
00:17:14.366 --> 00:17:18.500
Sorry to interrupt your activities. Resume, Clemont!

311
00:17:20.233 --> 00:17:21.233
Blaziken!

312
00:17:21.300 --> 00:17:24.166
Uh! Good job, Clembot! Get a good rest.

313
00:17:24.233 --> 00:17:26.099
You deserve it, after all.

314
00:17:26.166 --> 00:17:27.833
You too, Heliolisk!

315
00:17:27.900 --> 00:17:30.766
You leave me with no choice.

316
00:17:30.833 --> 00:17:33.633
-Magnezone!

317
00:17:33.700 --> 00:17:36.400
- Out of the way!
- Please, I want to handle this.

318
00:17:36.466 --> 00:17:38.166
- But wait.
- He'll be just fine.

319
00:17:38.233 --> 00:17:39.733
- Huh?
- Clemont knows what to do!

320
00:17:39.800 --> 00:17:42.433
All right, Luxray. Let's go!

321
00:17:44.533 --> 00:17:47.800
- Ray!
- Magnezone! Zap Cannon!

322
00:17:47.866 --> 00:17:49.900
Magnezone!

323
00:17:49.966 --> 00:17:52.466
- Quick, Luxray! Dodge it! Go!
- Ray!

324
00:17:52.533 --> 00:17:56.166
- Use Wild Charge!
- Luxray!

325
00:17:59.800 --> 00:18:03.566
What do you think you're doing? Hurry and get up! Electro Ball!

326
00:18:03.700 --> 00:18:06.300
Magnezone!

327
00:18:06.366 --> 00:18:08.700
Now, Luxray, hit that back with Swift!

328
00:18:08.766 --> 00:18:10.366
Lux!

329
00:18:12.833 --> 00:18:15.933
Hit that back with Tackle! And do it right now!

330
00:18:17.433 --> 00:18:19.366
- Not again.
- Terrible!

331
00:18:20.166 --> 00:18:23.100
- Magne!
- Luxray, dodge it and use Swift!

332
00:18:23.166 --> 00:18:25.500
Ray!

333
00:18:25.566 --> 00:18:28.366
Magne...

334
00:18:28.433 --> 00:18:31.500
..zone.

335
00:18:33.333 --> 00:18:37.866
I know your style. I learned it from watching Dark Clembot's battle.

336
00:18:37.933 --> 00:18:39.766
That's how I predicted your moves.

337
00:18:39.833 --> 00:18:45.333
From now on, I suggest you treat your robot and Pokémon with more respect!

338
00:18:45.400 --> 00:18:47.333
I knew you could beat them!

339
00:18:47.400 --> 00:18:49.166
What a cool big brother!

340
00:18:49.233 --> 00:18:50.433
Denne-ne.

341
00:18:51.166 --> 00:18:54.500
Doctor Belmondo, you're under arrest!

342
00:18:57.066 --> 00:18:58.933
Ash! Clemont!

343
00:18:59.000 --> 00:19:02.366
You two are going to have a Gym Battle, aren't you?

344
00:19:02.433 --> 00:19:05.000
- Huh?
- Hey! How did you know about that?

345
00:19:05.066 --> 00:19:07.933
I know everything that goes on in this city.

346
00:19:08.000 --> 00:19:09.966
Blaziken! Blaz! Blaz!

347
00:19:10.066 --> 00:19:12.600
Good luck to both of you!

348
00:19:12.666 --> 00:19:13.733
Ah! Wait!

349
00:19:14.633 --> 00:19:17.033
Ken!

350
00:19:17.100 --> 00:19:19.000
Argh! Slow down!

351
00:19:19.066 --> 00:19:21.233
He must still be around here. Let's go!

352
00:19:26.766 --> 00:19:30.233
Clemont, I'm looking forward to your Gym Battle.

353
00:19:30.300 --> 00:19:32.966
It's you against Ash. Man-to-man.

354
00:19:33.033 --> 00:19:35.533
It's time you fulfil the promise you made to him!

355
00:19:35.600 --> 00:19:38.533
Give it your all. Everything you've got!

356
00:19:38.600 --> 00:19:40.533
Blaziken.

357
00:19:49.200 --> 00:19:52.500
Now, I want you to eat as much as you'd like.

358
00:19:52.566 --> 00:19:54.300
There's plenty more where that came from!

359
00:19:54.366 --> 00:19:56.866
Thanks so much for the food! Yeah!

360
00:19:56.933 --> 00:19:59.866
Mm! It's yummy!

361
00:19:59.933 --> 00:20:02.866
- Pika, pika!
- Denne!

362
00:20:02.933 --> 00:20:05.866
Wow, they wrote about what happened yesterday!

363
00:20:05.933 --> 00:20:08.966
"The Lumiose Gym's Clembot was proven innocent.

364
00:20:09.033 --> 00:20:12.633
And for nabbing the real culprits, Clembot was given full honours!"

365
00:20:12.700 --> 00:20:14.366
Oh, let's see.

366
00:20:14.433 --> 00:20:16.966
That sounds like Alexa wrote that article!

367
00:20:17.033 --> 00:20:20.966
Say. Serena, you're right! This is amazing!

368
00:20:21.033 --> 00:20:23.300
And look at you. You're famous!

369
00:20:23.366 --> 00:20:25.466
Stop it. You're embarrassing me!

370
00:20:25.533 --> 00:20:29.100
- Now we can finally rest easy.
- Then today is the day?

371
00:20:29.166 --> 00:20:32.500
- Yup. Time for our Gym Battle!
- Pika.

372
00:20:32.566 --> 00:20:36.033
Although Clembot was arrested for crimes it didn't commit,

373
00:20:36.100 --> 00:20:39.266
our heroes figured out the identity of the true culprits.

374
00:20:39.333 --> 00:20:43.766
Now, Ash and Clemont's Gym Battle can finally get underway,

375
00:20:43.833 --> 00:20:46.766
as our heroes' journey continues!
